<title>USA: TABLE - Sola Q1 June 30 shr rises to $0.44.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Sola Q1 June 30 shr rises to $0.44.</headline>
<dateline>MENLO PARK, Calif. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sola International Inc</p>
<p>Unaudited (Amounts in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>						First Qtr	 First Qtr</p>
<p>						     1998		1997</p>
<p> Net sales				   $137,621	  $109,536</p>
<p>   Gross profit				64,827	    51,487</p>
<p>Research and development</p>
<p>    expenses				    4,755	     4,207</p>
<p>   Operating expenses			43,570	    45,405</p>
<p>   Operating income			  21,257	     6,082</p>
<p> Net income				    11,089	     2,162</p>
<p> Net income per share			  0.44		0.09</p>
<p>Weighted average number</p>
<p> of shares outstanding		     25,419	    23,159</p>
<p>					 Adjustments	   First Qtr</p>
<p>					    (1)(2)(3)		1997,</p>
<p>								 as adjusted</p>
<p> Net sales							$109,536</p>
<p>   Gross profit				 730	     52,217</p>
<p>Research and development</p>
<p>    expenses							 4,207</p>
<p>   Operating expenses		   (9,500)	     35,905</p>
<p>   Operating income			10,230	     16,312</p>
<p> Net income				   6,761		8,923</p>
<p> Net income per share					     0.39</p>
<p>Weighted average number</p>
<p>  of shares outstanding					 23,159</p>
<p>(1) Adjustment to cost of sales to remove the non-recurring</p>
<p>charge of $730K amortization for 10 days of a step-up of</p>
<p>inventories to fair value arising from the AO acquisition. The remainder of the step-up of inventories to fair value (total step-up is $7.2 million) was amortized through cost of sales in the second quarter of fiscal 1997.</p>
<p>(2) Adjustment to eliminate in-process research &amp; development expense associated with the AO acquisition, as it is non-recurring.</p>
<p>(3) Adjustment to provision for income taxes to tax effect the adjustments in (1) and (2) above.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
